<header class="page-head">
  <h1>Record an entry</h1>
  <p class="sub">Money moves <em>from</em> one account <em>to</em> another. finfry builds the balanced pair of postings.</p>
</header>

<form class="entry" method="post" action="/record" data-record>
  <label class="wide">Memo
    <input list="memos" name="memo" placeholder="Coffee" autofocus autocomplete="off" data-recall>
    <span class="field-note">A memo you've used before fills in the rest — only blanks, never what you've typed.</span>
  </label>
  <label>Amount <input name="amount" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="12.50" required></label>
  <label>Date <input type="date" name="date" value="<%= @today %>"></label>
  <label>To <input list="to-accounts" name="to" placeholder="Expenses:Food:Coffee" required autocomplete="off"></label>
  <label>From <input list="from-accounts" name="from" value="<%= h @funding %>" required autocomplete="off"></label>
  <label>Recurs <select name="recurrence"><option value="">no</option><%= cadence_options %></select></label>
  <p class="kind wide" data-kind aria-live="polite"></p>
  <button type="submit" class="primary" data-submit>Record</button>
</form>
<datalist id="memos"><% @memos.each do |m| %><option value="<%= h m %>"></option><% end %></datalist>
<datalist id="to-accounts"><%= account_options to_accounts %></datalist>
<datalist id="from-accounts"><%= account_options from_accounts %></datalist>

<p class="hint">Any pair of accounts works: <code>Expenses:*</code> as the destination is an expense, <code>Income:*</code> as the source is income, anything else is a transfer — a card payment is from Checking to the card; a refund is from the expense back to Checking. Splits across several accounts are recorded from the command line: <code>finfry add -m "market run" Expenses:Food:Groceries 42 Expenses:Food:Snacks 8 Assets:Checking</code>.</p>
